    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "conclusions: Most studies in this updated review targeted the prevalence of limitations of functioning of rehabilitation interest in coVID-19 survivors. This is similar to past review findings; however, data in the new studies was collected at longer follow-up periods (up to one year after symptom onset) and in larger samples of participants. More rcts and analytical observational studies are available, but the methodological quality of recently published studies is low. There is a need for good quality intervention efficacy and effectiveness studies to complement the rapidly expanding evidence from observational studies.",
      "reason": "The abstract describes what the existing evidence shows (focus on prevalence/natural history, low methodological quality) and identifies uncertainties/gaps (need for good quality intervention efficacy/effectiveness studies)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "The best available research evidence is required to inform management and rehabilitation decisions, interventions, and health systems for COVID-19 survivors with adverse clinical sequelae. Further evidence is warranted to estimate the resources needed to plan for setting appropriate and adequately delivered post-acute and long-term rehabilitation services.",
      "reason": "The introduction text explains why conducting/using the review evidence is important (to inform management/rehabilitation decisions and to estimate resources for post-acute/long-term services)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_15",
      "quote": "The literature search was comprehensive with the search strategy replicating previous review editions that, to date, have been the most complete investigations of rehabilitation evidence related to COVID in health literature.",
      "reason": "The review states the search replicates previous review editions and that prior findings are similar, but the evidence provided does not clearly identify and cite specific “previous systematic reviews” (with explicit references) to justify the need for this current review/update."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No evidence was retrieved describing a proposed mechanism of action of the intervention(s) in the context of intervention effects."
    },
    {
